{"id":"word:hebrew:H3920","type":"word","title":"לָכַד","subtitle":"H3920 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to catch (in a net, trap or pit); generally, to capture or occupy; also to choose (by lot); figuratively, to cohere","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לָכַד (H3920) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 121 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לָכַד (lâkad) means to catch (in a net, trap or pit); generally, to capture or occupy; also to choose (by lot); figuratively, to cohere First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 5."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לָכַד","transliteration":"lâkad","pronunciation":"law-kad'","strong":"H3920","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3920","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יִּלְכֹּ֤ד","וַ/יִּלָּכֵ֖ד","וַֽ/יִּלְכְּדָֽ/הּ","נִלְכְּדָ֣ה","נִלְכְּדָ֖ה"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3ms",18],["HVqp3ms",11],["HVNp3fs",10],["HC/Vqw3mp",10],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3fs",9],["HC/VNw3ms",7],["HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3fs",5],["HC/Vqq3ms/Sp3fs",5],["HVNi3ms",3],["HC/VNq3cp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to catch (in a net, trap or pit); generally, to capture or occupy; also to choose (by lot); figuratively, to cohere","usage":"× at all, catch (self), be frozen, be holden, stick together, take.","full":"H3920. lakad לָכַד 121 verb capture, seize, take (by lot) (Phoenician לכד take out, choose (?); לְכַד ᵑ7 as Biblical Hebrew; Arabic is strike, push , with the hand, etc., pestle , compare modern attack Wetzst ZMG xxii. 1868, 140 ; stick or cleave to); — Qal Perfect ׳ל Josh 8:1 +, לָכַדְתִּי 2Sam 12:27 etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִלְכּוֺד Amos 3:5 ; וַיִּלְכֹּד Judg 8:12 +, etc.; Imperative masculine singular suffix לָכְדָהּ 2Sam 12:28 , masculine plural לִכְדוּ ; Infinitive absolute לָכוֺד Amos 3:5 ; construct suffix לְלָכְדֵנִי Jer 18:22 , לְלָכְדָהּ 32:24 ; Participle לֹכֵד Job 5:13 ; Prov 16:32 ; &#8212; 1 capture, seize (not in P) with accusative, usually a city or town, in war Judg 1:8 , 12 ; Josh 8:21 ; 10:1 (JE), Deut 2:35 48t. (but Judg 1:18 strike out as gloss Bu Kit GFM and others); land Josh 10:42 (D), Dan 11:18 ; water-courses (fords), Judg 3:28 ; 7:24 (twice in verse); 12:8 ; object men (usually princes, kings) in battle 7:25 ; 8:12 , 14 ; Josh 11:12 , 17 (D), 2Chr 22:9 ; 33:11 ; captives and spoils 2Sam 8:4 = 1Chr 18:4 ; of Saul's seizing the kingdom ( הַמְּלוּכָה ), i.e. acquiring it actually by force of arms 1Sam 14:47 ; also of Samson's catching the foxes Judg 15:4 ; of a lion catching his prey Amos 3:4 ; of a trap, snare, יִלְכּוֺד לָכוֺד 3:5 . 2 figurative of entrapping men Jer 5:26 ; Psa 35:8 , compare Prov 5:22 ; Job 5:13 and (of a pit) Jer 18:22 . 3 of taking by lot Josh 7:14 (3 t. in verse); 7:17 (J E; see Niph`al 3 ). Niph`al Perfect נִלְכַּד Lam 4:20 ; 3 feminine singular נִלְכְּדָה 1Kin 16:18 +, etc.; Imperfect יִלָּכֵד Isa 24:18 ; Jer 48:44 ; כָּהּ יִלָּ֫כֶד Eccl 7:26 ; וַיִּלָּכֵד Josh 7:16 +, etc.; Participle נִלְכָּד 7:15 ; &#8212; 1 be captured in war, of city 1Kin 16:18 ; 2Kin 18:10 ; Jer 38:28 (twice in verse); 48:1 , 41 ; 50:2 , 9 , 24 ; 51:31 , 41 ; Zech 14:2 ; of men Jer 51:56 ; Lam 4:20 (compare Qal 1 ). 2 of men, be caught , namely, in a snare or trap, only figurative, usually by divine judgment Isa 8:15 ; 24:18 ; 28:13 ; Psa 9:16 ; 59:13 ; Prov 6:2 ; 11:6 ; Jer 6:11 ; 8:9 ; so of Moab 48:7 , 44 ; of being ensnared by a woman Eccl 7:26 ; of being caught by cords of distress, עֹ֑נִי בְּחַבְלֵי , Job 36:8 . 3 be taken by lot Josh 7:15-16 , 17 , 18 (all J E), 1Sam 10:20-21 , (twice in verse); 14:41-42 , (compare Qal 3 ). Hithpa`el Imperfect 3masculine plural; יִתְמָּרָ֑דוּ וְלֹא יִתְלַכְּדוּ Job 41:9 they grasp each other, and cannot be separated , of crocodile's scales (|| יְדֻבָּ֑קוּ בְּאָחִיהוּ אִישׁ ); יִתְלַכָּ֑דוּ תְהוֺם מְּנֵי 38:30 the face of the deep compacts (of freezing; || יִתְחַבָּ֑אוּ מַיִם כָּאֶבֶן ; verbs transposed, plausibly, by Me Bi Siegf Bu).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 11 5","keyReferences":["1Chr 11 5","1Chr 18 4","1Kgs 9 16","1Kgs 16 18","1Sam 10 20","1Sam 10 21","1Sam 10 21","1Sam 14 41"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":121,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 11 5","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלְכֹּ֤ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 18 4","book":"1Chr","chapter":18,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלְכֹּד֩","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 9 16","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלְכֹּ֤ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 16 18","book":"1Kgs","chapter":16,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נִלְכְּדָ֣ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVNp3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 20","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלָּכֵ֖ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/VNw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 21","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תִּלָּכֵ֖ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/VNw3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 21","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלָּכֵד֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/VNw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 41","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":41,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלָּכֵ֧ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/VNw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 42","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלָּכֵ֖ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/VNw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 14 47","book":"1Sam","chapter":14,"verse":47,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לָכַ֥ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3ms"},{"reference":"2Chr 12 4","book":"2Chr","chapter":12,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּלְכֹּ֛ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"2Chr 13 19","b